# The application-grid launcher for the snap.
#
# Its absence was a first-run cliff, not a cosmetic gap. Four apps were declared
# in snapcraft.yaml and not one carried a `desktop:` key, so snapd exported
# nothing to /var/lib/snapd/desktop/applications/ — firefox, vlc and snap-store
# are all there, yazses was not. Anyone installing from App Center, KDE Discover
# or the snapcraft.io web button therefore finished the install with nothing to
# click and no indication that a terminal was required.
#
# It opens the settings window rather than starting dictation, for the reason
# the Flathub launcher records: an activation from an app grid has no terminal,
# and hold-to-talk is a background daemon with nothing to show. A launcher that
# appears to do nothing is worse than a launcher that opens the one window where
# the hotkey, the microphone and every capability can be set — and, in a snap,
# it is also the one surface that can say the interfaces are not connected.
#
# Exec must name the snap's own command so snapd will rewrite it to
# /snap/bin/yazses; an absolute path here is rejected at build time.
#
# `desktop-file-validate` reports the ${SNAP} Icon as "looks like a relative
# path". That warning applies to every snap and is expected: snapd rewrites
# ${SNAP} to the mount point at export time. Verified against the installed
# snaps on a real machine -- firefox ships `Icon=${SNAP}/default256.png` and
# vlc `Icon=${SNAP}/usr/share/icons/.../vlc.png`, and the exported copies read
# `Icon=/snap/firefox/current/default256.png`. Do not "fix" it to a bare icon
# name: the host icon theme does not search inside the snap, so the launcher
# would render with no icon at all.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=YazSes
GenericName=Voice dictation
Comment=Offline voice dictation — hold a key, speak, and your words are typed
Exec=yazses settings
Icon=${SNAP}/meta/gui/yazses.png
Terminal=false
Categories=Utility;Accessibility;
Keywords=voice;dictation;speech;transcription;accessibility;microphone;typing;
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=yazses
